>
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Periodontal disease is associated with cardiovascular disease, diabetes, cognitive
    decline, and systemic inflammatory burden — yet most men treat dental care as cosmetic
    maintenance rather than a health priority. The Mitigate pillar includes oral health
    because the mouth is a direct window into whole-body inflammatory status.
  </p>
  <p>
    This isn't about flossing lectures. It's about understanding that chronic oral dysbiosis
    creates a persistent low-grade inflammatory load that undermines every other protocol
    you're running. Address it once, maintain it consistently, and it stops being a headwind.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Baseline Assessment</h3>
      <p>Know your periodontal status. A full-mouth probing is the only way to understand what's actually happening.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Oral Microbiome Support</h3>
      <p>Diet quality, nasal breathing, and avoiding harsh antiseptic mouthwashes support a healthy oral microbiome.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Sleep Apnea Screen</h3>
      <p>Bruxism and dental wear patterns often indicate sleep-disordered breathing — a major cardiovascular risk.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Systemic Connection</h3>
      <p>Gut health (Biome-AF protocol) and oral health reinforce each other — the microbiome is contiguous.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SolutionPage>
